{"author":{"id":"89da5fec8eff6d69dbcdd68f81be7e9163b16f34b17e978ecf3554487379f453"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1773940493,"nonce":"POyieHHmlKxgQwYjqpwivGoFHwQ=","message":"**Truncation fix approach**: The truncation logic should be Markdown-aware. When truncating a string that contains inline Markdown spans:\n\n- Parse or detect open inline spans (backtick fences, `**`, `_`, etc.) before truncating\n- If truncation falls inside an open span, either:\n  (a) Extend the span to cover the truncated portion and append an ellipsis inside the span (e.g. `/some/long/pa…` rendered as monospace with ellipsis), or\n  (b) Close the span at the truncation point and append a styled ellipsis\n\nOption (a) is preferred — it preserves the visual intent (the user sees a monospace-formatted truncated path rather than raw syntax).\n\nThis likely means introducing a 'truncate then rebalance Markdown spans' utility, or alternatively, rendering Markdown first and then truncating the rendered output (measuring on the DOM or on the formatted string rather than the raw source).","files":null}]}